  RESULT
================================================================================

  chain                           R-1   flat  total   fraction
  dyad_mnu  (CONVERGED)         0.176      0      9        0%
  conv_desi (stuck)             13.25      0      9        0%
  zon_disp  (stuck)              23.3      0      9        0%
  zon       (stuck)             40.36      0      9        0%

  converged control : 0% of directions barely constrained
  stuck chains      : 0%

  DIRECTION: no separation. Weak evidence against, with the same caveat.

  THE SHARPER READING, from the per-chain rankings above.

  The hypothesis names its suspects: 'the zon and dCDF parameters'. They are
  not merely un-flat -- dcdf_rho_inf is the NARROWEST direction in every one
  of the three stuck chains (r = 0.010, 0.012, 0.012), and log10_zon sits
  mid-pack. The named suspects behave OPPOSITE to the prediction.

  And the shape is wrong in a second way. A chain crawling along a genuine flat
  valley should be WIDE in that direction and narrow elsewhere -- it moves
  freely where the likelihood is level. What the stuck chains actually show is
  narrow in EVERY direction, uniformly ~3.5x narrower than the converged
  control. That is the signature of a chain not moving at all, not of one
  wandering a flat valley.

  WHAT THIS STILL CANNOT DO, and why it is not a refutation. It compares
  widths, not mixing, and the understatement bias (F-D) is 3.5x -- larger than
  any plausible signal. A chain stuck badly enough would fail to explore even a
  genuinely flat direction, which would produce exactly this picture. So the
  hypothesis is UNSUPPORTED and its named suspects are excluded, but the
  general claim survives as untested.

  WHAT WOULD SETTLE IT. Not a re-read of finished chains -- the bias is
  intrinsic to them. Either (a) the likelihood's curvature at the best fit,
  which is a property of the posterior rather than of any chain's wandering,
  or (b) a short well-tuned run on the same parameter set. Both are real work
  and neither is attempted here.
================================================================================
